===Etymology===
From {{af|ru|пе́чь|t1=to bake|-е́нье}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*peťì}}, from {{inh|ru|ine-bsl-pro|*pektei}}, from {{inh|ru|ine-pro|*pékʷeti}}, from the root {{m|ine-pro|*pekʷ-}}, whence English {{m|en|cook}} and {{m|en|biscuit}} (in part).

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|пече́нье|pos=n}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-печенье.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|пече́нье|dim=пече́нька,печеню́шка|expr=печеню́ха}}

# [[pastry]], [[cruller]]
# {{sense|UK}} [[biscuit]]; {{sense|US}} [[cookie]]
# [[cracker]]

